  "baseline_policy": "Conservative audited coverage: generated metadata/schema, spawn/default, and the source-derived transform/interpolation family partition apply to every catalog row. Generic callback, rendering, event, and debug implementations do not prove their remaining composite cells, so those stay partial until a family slice proves the whole cell. Vanilla NoopRenderer registrations are narrow model not-applicable exceptions.",
  "uncertainties": [
    "Generic passenger state is present, but family-specific attachment, controlling-passenger, equipment applicability, and leash presentation have not been reverse-audited together.",
    "Generated dimensions and broad pick tests exist, but each pose/scale/collision exception has not been proven for every family.",
    "Renderer and animation coverage is extensive, but no reverse proof yet shows that every non-noop EntityRenderers registration has exact model, texture, layers, and animation.",
    "Entity-event coverage has many focused mappings, but the complete vanilla subclass override inventory is still open.",
    "Shift-local save projection covers many families, but server-private versus client-observable fields still need a family-by-family audit."
  ],
